Found by the k69 worker (2026-11-21): the agent exit prompt creates a new bufio.Scanner on stdin each time; a scanner can buffer past the line it returns, so with piped stdin later input can be lost. A terminal is not affected. Done when: one reader is shared for the session, with a pipe test. Lane: unreagent-worker. Touches cmd/launcher/lifecycle.go — after k69/k70/k71 lands.

2026-11-21 08:59 Worker: cause confirmed with a red test (TestPipedInputReachesThePromptAndThenTheConsole: one piped write 'k/status/q', the prompt's Scanner took all three lines, the console never saw 'q'). Fix: console.in is now one lineReader made once in run() (newConsole) and shared by the exit prompt, the k-console and run()'s own commandLoop. It reads a byte at a time and never past the line it returns, so nothing is lost between prompt and console, nor at the k71 handover to the foreground agent, which reads the same stdin itself. Pin: TestConsoleReaderTakesNoMoreThanItsLine. Windows console reads 1 UTF-16 unit per ReadConsole call this way: compile-only, unverified.

